1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,800
THE CHARACTERS, RACES,
AND LOCATIONS ARE FICTIONAL.

2
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,720
THE HISTORY OF MINORITY STRUGGLES IS REAL.

3
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,960
Why is it Mintada and Siprai
who get to study in Thailand

4
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,240
<i>instead of me?!</i>

5
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,320
We won't stand by and let them climb over.

6
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:56,240
We will never allow them
to bring it into Thailand.

7
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,480
Freeze! Hands up.

8
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,160
As thorough as we check,

9
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:07,440
<i>those bastards always</i>
<i>find a way to pull off a drug run.</i>

10
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:13,120
-Siprai.
-Can't you see people walking?

11
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:14,400
I'm so sorry.

12
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:25,280
-Let's see.
-Hello.

13
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,600
Do they have snacks?

14
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,120
-It doesn't exist, Yoon.
-How? This place is big.

15
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,640
-So many people here.
-Yeah.

16
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,800
-No way.
-They even have a drama club.

17
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,920
-So many clubs.
-No cheering club. Too tired.

18
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,640
-Sorry.
-Hey.

19
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,200
I wanna join the conservation club.

20
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,720
Conservation? Conservation of what?
Pots, pans, antiques, stuff like that?

21
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,920
The Nature Conservation Club!

22
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,440
You know, joining this club
means going on trips too.

23
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,960
Really? Then sign me up right away.

24
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,000
-Let's go.
-You sure?

25
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,000
-We're signing up.
-Welcome.

26
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:53,960
-Okay.
-Here you go.

27
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,680
Sign here?

28
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,720
-Let me see where are the trips to?
-Thank you.

29
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,080
Club recruitment's open. Interested?

30
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:04,520
-We're joining.
-Signing up? We're the drama club.

31
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,520
Sign in what language?

32
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,520
Thai.

33
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,600
Or if you’re not Thai,
English is fine too.

34
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:16,200
If English doesn’t work either,
what nationality are you then? Sawin?

35
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:22,080
I’m not Sawin. I’m Kase.

36
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,440
-Siprai…
-Kase?

37
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,760
What, is being Kase
a big problem or something?

38
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:31,000
No. Just write in Kase then.

39
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,240
I'm not joining anymore.

40
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,480
-Calling me a Sawin?
-Siprai.

41
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:37,920
-Typical Kase, always so radical.
-Sign here.

42
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:43,000
-Let's sign up quickly and get going.
-Yeah.

43
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:47,200
Alright, That's it for
intro to political science today.

44
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,600
The next class will get much more intense.

45
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:52,800
And a quick warning
for anyone skipping class,

46
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,520
miss more than three classes,

47
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,120
and you’re disqualified from the exam.
Understood?

48
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,680
Yes, Ma'am.

49
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,240
Okay, that’s all for today.

50
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:04,600
Siprai…

51
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,959
Siprai, you idiot.

52
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,000
Hey, you!

53
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:23,440
-Quick! Come with me right now.
-What happened?

54
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:26,000
-Your friend's beating up another student.
-Where?

55
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:31,440
Let go of me.

56
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,320
-Siprai, stop.
-Why don't you fight back?

57
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,800
-Siprai, stop!
-Ongdee!

58
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:40,280
Siprai, what the hell did you just do?

59
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,840
He’s Sawin.

60
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,240
Yes, I am Sawin.

61
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:49,760
But if you punch me
just because I’m Sawin,

62
00:04:50,280 --> 00:04:52,440
you're no better than
the Sawin soldiers you hate.

63
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,560
Our countries might be at war,

64
00:04:56,920 --> 00:05:00,640
but that doesn’t mean
every Kase and Sawin must be enemies.

65
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,480
Even so, we can never be friends!

66
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:03,440
Siprai!

67
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:05,200
Why not?

68
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,040
Friendship in times of conflict

69
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,440
is invaluable to humanity

70
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:14,360
whether you're Kase,
Sawin, or anyone else.

71
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:22,280
Drink up. It'll help you calm down.

72
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,080
I don't get it.

73
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,440
Just introducing myself got me punched.

74
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,680
Man, you're really hot-headed, Siprai.

75
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:36,400
Apologize to Ongdee right now.

76
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,480
Say it!

77
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,520
I’m sorry.

78
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,240
I'm sorry too.

79
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,560
I didn't expect
Siprai to be so hot-headed.

80
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,800
Anyway, is there
a reason you came to see us?

81
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:55,240
There's an annual
international performance

82
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,960
for students from
all over, to showcase their talents.

83
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:02,080
I'm the head of the Sawin students.
So I'd like to ask you two to join us.

84
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,200
Why should I join?

85
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,040
Watch your tongue, man.

86
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,080
You decide, Mintada.

87
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,000
We're in.

88
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,720
Hey.

89
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:20,040
Great. This will be the very first time

90
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,880
we'll have a Kase's performance.

91
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:25,480
You two think it over
and decide what you want to show.

92
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,120
Sure.

93
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,720
Chart, keep this in mind.

94
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,760
Women love surprises,

95
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,720
especially a sweet one.

96
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:39,600
No matter how mad or upset she is,
it's all gone in an instant.

97
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:44,120
How about this? Chart, do you remember

98
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,800
the exact day you first met Irene?

99
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,400
I remember it vividly.

100
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,200
It's the day I got shot.

101
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,000
And today is our one-month anniversary.

102
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:58,840
So let's pull off a surprise
for the anniversary of when you met.

103
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,880
Perfect timing!

104
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:01,240
A surprise? Today?

105
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:05,080
Wouldn't three months be better, Sa?

106
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:08,960
Three months is way too long.
Let’s do it today.

107
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,520
Today? We won’t make it in time. Trust me.

108
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:14,240
Chart, I'm young and impatient.
We do it today!

109
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,680
There's no time, Sa.

110
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:18,280
We’ll make it.
Trust me. I’ll help you out.

111
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,520
-We won't make it, Sa.
-Hey.

112
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,800
-Not if you keep dragging your feet.
-For real?

113
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,840
Let’s go!

114
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:28,560
Irene, I saw someone loitering
near the elevator the other day.

115
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:30,680
He looked pretty suspicious.

116
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,760
You should be careful.

117
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,200
Thanks, Nate.

118
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,360
I’m taking off now.

119
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:38,080
Alright, get home safely.

120
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,520
Tiger One, target has stepped out.

121
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,160
Tiger Two, stall her. We aren’t ready yet.

122
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:50,840
I’ll try but I don’t know
how long I can hold her off.

123
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,720
Stall her as long as you can.

124
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:55,040
Okay, but you’d better hurry up.

125
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:57,320
I’m moving as fast as I can. Gotta go.

126
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:01,600
Chart, hurry up.

127
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,720
I am.

128
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,960
Faster.

129
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,640
Where should I put this?

130
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,400
-Here? No.
-Give me.

131
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,520
Right here.

132
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,360
Irene. Irene.

133
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,960
Irene, wait a moment.

134
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:17,320
Chet, is something wrong?

135
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,320
Well…

136
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:23,120
It's Chart.

137
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:27,160
Chart isn’t feeling well.
He sent me to pick you up for him.

138
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:32,400
I can't help with that.
You should take Chart to see a doctor.

139
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,120
Wait a moment, Irene.

140
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,440
Is there anything else?

141
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,640
Uh…

142
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,240
Nothing else. Please go ahead.

143
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:51,880
Tiger One, mission failed.
I could not stall the target.

144
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,200
Damn it.

145
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,920
Is Irene almost here?

146
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,680
Yes. What do we do, Sa?

147
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,520
Wait, Chart.

148
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,840
Go change your clothes now.

149
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,080
-Hurry.
-Change my clothes?

150
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,800
-Yes. I’ll handle this.
-Okay.

151
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,160
Please be quick.

152
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,840
Fish, put here.

153
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,160
Is it gonna work?

154
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:34,000
Of course it is.

155
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,000
It's our anniversary.

156
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,160
You remembered?

157
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,960
I hope you’ll forgive me.

158
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,560
For what?

159
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:41,360
For putting work first.

160
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,040
You’ve got it wrong.

161
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,880
Then what's--

162
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,680
It's my Commander.

163
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,520
You should answer it.

164
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,440
Hello, Commander.

165
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:31,720
Our job here is done. Let's go.

166
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,720
Yup.

167
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,760
-Wait, Sa.
-Huh?

168
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,320
-Why?
-No idea.

169
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,160
I have to go now.

170
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:49,960
Alright.

171
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,400
Chart, what happened?

172
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,480
Chet,

173
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,760
the Mothulas we caught
the other day escaped.

174
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:27,280
We have to move now.

175
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,280
Hold on, Chart.

176
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:31,480
You can stay here.
I’ll explain to the Commander.

177
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:32,680
I can’t do that.

178
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:36,800
I’m heading out, Sa.
Please keep an eye on Irene.

179
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,760
Irene…

180
00:12:58,240 --> 00:12:59,120
Sa.

181
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:09,240
Please don’t be mad at Chart.

182
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,360
He’s like this

183
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:17,080
because he grew up in a military family.

184
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,240
You don’t need to explain, I understand.

185
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:23,160
As a nurse and a soldier myself,

186
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,520
I have to make sacrifices for work too.

187
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,880
Then why haven’t you been
picking up Chart’s calls lately?

188
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:33,440
I don't want him
to get in trouble because of me.

189
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,560
Trouble?

190
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:46,600
IRENE ROJKAROON

191
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:57,000
IF YOU DON'T DUMP
THAT CAPTAIN, I'LL KILL HIM.

192
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,080
It couldn't be anyone but Prapt.

193
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:00,600
Huh?

194
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:02,600
We used to date

195
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:04,800
before I met Chart.

196
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:08,480
Do you really think he’d dare to do it?

197
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,800
I’m not sure

198
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,600
but no matter what,

199
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,560
I won’t let Chart get hurt because of me.

200
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,560
We should tell Chart.

201
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,560
So that's why.

202
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,640
I’m sorry for not telling you earlier.

203
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:40,920
It’s just an empty threat.

204
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
I’m not so sure.

205
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,720
Prapt has friends who are drug dealers.

206
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:48,200
He might do something crazy.

207
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:50,160
In that case, we must be extra careful.

208
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,720
I can’t hear a thing, Chet.

209
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,240
NAME LIST

210
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:38,720
-Yiaza.
-The head is out.

211
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,040
Hang in there, Yiaza.

212
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,120
Just a little more.

213
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,080
Push it. One, two, three.

214
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:45,360
Like that.

215
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:47,840
-Push hard, push hard.
-Is it out, Grandma?

216
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,640
-Is it out?
-Almost there.

217
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:53,440
-The head is out, Yiaza.
-I can't take it.

218
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:54,560
Here it comes.

219
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:56,560
Come on.

220
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:57,880
Yeah!

221
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,400
It’s out, Yiaza.

222
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:01,240
It’s out.

223
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,680
Yiaza.

224
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:03,680
The warriors are back.

225
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:16,319
Colonel Layee! Colonel Layee!

226
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,200
Yiaza! Yiaza!

227
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:20,079
What's wrong with Yiaza?

228
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,720
-Yiaza gave birth.
-Huh?

229
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,440
Yep, she gave birth.

230
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:32,720
Look who’s smiling.

231
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,360
Who’s smiling?

232
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,800
Smile.

233
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,920
Yiaza, I’m back.

234
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,480
Aren’t you tired?

235
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,960
Not at all.
Right now, I’m happier than ever.

236
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,120
Yiaza.

237
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:03,280
Hold him.

238
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:06,840
I don’t dare to.

239
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,440
I’m only used to holding guns.

240
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:16,440
The baby will feel safe
in its father’s arms.

241
00:18:23,760 --> 00:18:25,720
Your arms.

242
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:30,920
Look.

243
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,440
Mind the neck.

244
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,360
THE ASEAN HANDBOOK

245
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,280
My wife is so beautiful.

246
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:56,760
Now that I’ve had a child,

247
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,320
I won’t look young or pretty anymore.

248
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,320
My love for you

249
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,400
and our child will never change.

250
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:10,160
Yiaza.

251
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,720
What should we name him?

252
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,920
I stayed up all night thinking about it.

253
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,200
How about Laza?

254
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,000
Hm?

255
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:24,240
Your name is Yiaza and mine is Layee,

256
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:27,360
so our child will have
both our names together.

257
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,760
Laza?

258
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:33,280
You don’t like it?

259
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:36,920
Don’t just laugh, Yiaza.

260
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,400
Help me think.

261
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,040
What name do you like, Son?

262
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,440
What should we name him?

263
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:46,200
Layee. Yiaza.

264
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,200
Dad.

265
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:02,000
I brought sacred herbs and leaves.

266
00:21:03,360 --> 00:21:04,280
Thank you, Dad.

267
