-Nothing? Really?

519
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:02,080
What's the point to tune it now?

520
00:38:03,680 --> 00:38:05,000
Can’t keep his hands still.

521
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:14,760
I think the long-haired guy
is so handsome.

522
00:38:14,840 --> 00:38:18,080
So cool, rugged and attractive.

523
00:38:18,160 --> 00:38:20,920
So handsome, he caught my eye instantly.

524
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:23,960
But I think he’s too rugged.
The other one is cuter.

525
00:38:24,560 --> 00:38:26,280
Cute and adorable.

526
00:38:27,520 --> 00:38:29,200
No way, mine is the best.

527
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:31,760
How about we let Sa decide?

528
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:33,920
Sa.

529
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,320
-Sa.
-Sa.

530
00:38:40,120 --> 00:38:41,120
Why are you calling?

531
00:38:41,720 --> 00:38:43,320
You're daydreaming?

532
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:47,320
I was just thinking
about some marketing terms.

533
00:38:48,880 --> 00:38:49,720
No way.

534
00:38:49,800 --> 00:38:51,160
Spill it.

535
00:38:57,680 --> 00:39:01,320
I was thinking about
the song those Kase students sang.

536
00:39:03,520 --> 00:39:07,840
Thinking about the song,
or thinking about the singers?

537
00:39:07,920 --> 00:39:09,760
I really mean the song.

538
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:11,360
Really?

539
00:39:11,440 --> 00:39:13,840
At first, I didn’t think much of it.

540
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,520
But looking back,

541
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,160
though the melody sounded joyful,

542
00:39:18,240 --> 00:39:21,680
the singer's voice was tinged with sorrow.

543
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:25,040
Well, look at you getting all deep!

544
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:29,680
I'm serious.
It feels like they sang from the heart.

545
00:39:30,200 --> 00:39:34,160
The Kase people
must have been through so much.

546
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:42,040
MUNITIONS DEPOT

547
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:46,280
The Mothulas
love to act like flash floods.

548
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:49,360
Wherever there’s a gap,

549
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:51,560
they try to squeeze through.

550
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:53,200
Do you know how many entry points

551
00:39:53,920 --> 00:39:56,440
they use to smuggle drugs
into Thai territory?

552
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:01,840
Here,

553
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:04,760
here,

554
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:07,200
here,

555
00:40:08,160 --> 00:40:09,480
here,

556
00:40:10,720 --> 00:40:11,840
here,

557
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:14,640
and here.

558
00:40:19,240 --> 00:40:20,160
That’s why

559
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:23,800
no matter how many forces we deploy,

560
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:25,880
narcotics still manage to slip through.

561
00:40:26,600 --> 00:40:30,520
We'll need more than soldiers,
border guards, and forestry officers.

562
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:31,640
Exactly.

563
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:34,480
The best eyes and ears

564
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:36,680
are the locals.

565
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:38,920
If everyone cooperates,

566
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,520
our coverage will increase tremendously.

567
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:57,760
Be very careful out in the field.

568
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:01,320
We don't know who among
the villagers is good or bad,

569
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,200
or who might have infiltrated them.

570
00:41:03,280 --> 00:41:04,120
Yes.

571
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:07,040
But I still believe in good intentions.

572
00:41:08,600 --> 00:41:10,840
As a King’s soldier,

573
00:41:11,560 --> 00:41:15,200
our mission is
for the nation, the Monarchy

574
00:41:16,040 --> 00:41:17,360
and the people.

575
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:23,560
I believe in you as well.

576
00:41:50,520 --> 00:41:51,480
Soldiers incoming!

577
00:42:05,640 --> 00:42:06,800
Will this really work?

578
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:11,040
Just seeing military uniforms,
the locals run faster than seeing a ghost.

579
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:15,640
The villagers

580
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:19,160
might have bad memories
of soldiers or authority figures.

581
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:22,800
But since our intentions are good,
things are bound to work out.

582
00:42:22,880 --> 00:42:26,360
Right. Let's go talk
to the village chief first.

583
00:42:35,880 --> 00:42:36,760
Please leave.

584
00:42:36,840 --> 00:42:40,320
We can’t help you. It's hard enough
just making ends meet every day.

585
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:42,240
We aren’t asking for much.

586
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:45,680
If you notice anything unusual,
just report it to us.

587
00:42:45,760 --> 00:42:46,600
We'll handle it.

588
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:48,920
Nobody dares to report anything.

589
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:50,960
If they find out someone talked,

590
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:52,360
we’re dead meat.

591
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:54,520
Our relatives will get dragged down too.

592
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:56,400
You guys only bring trouble.

593
00:42:59,520 --> 00:43:00,760
Thank you anyway.

594
00:43:10,080 --> 00:43:11,080
Told you so.

595
00:43:11,160 --> 00:43:13,400
We even got called a jinx.

596
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:16,440
The mission just started,
and you've given up already?

597
00:43:17,680 --> 00:43:20,440
Chet, are you still with me?

598
00:43:20,520 --> 00:43:21,640
I am.

599
00:43:21,720 --> 00:43:23,760
We’ve faced far worse than this.

600
00:43:57,640 --> 00:43:58,720
Mintada.

601
00:44:01,280 --> 00:44:04,240
Siprai. Did you secretly follow me?

602
00:44:04,880 --> 00:44:06,240
What are you planning to do?

603
00:44:10,880 --> 00:44:12,160
Mintada.

604
00:44:14,480 --> 00:44:15,880
Mintada.

605
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:18,000
You're taking this too far.

606
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:20,800
You're like this
after seeing her just once?

607
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:24,240
I just wanna get to know her.

608
00:44:24,320 --> 00:44:26,080
Get to know her?

609
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:29,400
And you think
she'd want to know a Kase like you?

610
00:44:29,480 --> 00:44:31,920
That’s enough, Siprai. Enough.

611
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:33,920
Stop rubbing it in.

612
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:36,920
I know how worthless we are to Thais.

613
00:44:37,800 --> 00:44:39,520
Good. At least you know it.

614
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:41,480
Wait.

615
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:43,920
What else?

616
00:44:44,440 --> 00:44:47,640
I ran into Saemah,
and he passed a letter to you.

617
00:44:50,520 --> 00:44:51,960
A letter from Mom.

618
00:45:07,160 --> 00:45:08,520
What’s wrong, Siprai?

619
00:45:11,320 --> 00:45:13,800
I just wish someone
would write a letter to me too.

620
00:45:20,880 --> 00:45:24,480
My mom's letter isn't just for me.

621
00:45:24,560 --> 00:45:26,160
She wrote to you as well.

622
00:45:26,240 --> 00:45:27,320
Look.

623
00:45:31,440 --> 00:45:33,320
Come on.
Let’s find a place to sit and read.

624
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:39,440
<i>At first, we thought</i>

625
00:45:40,120 --> 00:45:43,080
<i>the attackers were</i>
<i>Sawin soldiers as usual,</i>

626
00:45:44,280 --> 00:45:45,960
<i>but this time it wasn't.</i>

627
00:45:47,120 --> 00:45:50,160
<i>Those who attacked us</i>
<i>weren't affiliated with the government</i>

628
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:53,400
<i>but were the Mothulas</i>

629
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,160
<i>trying to open up their drug route.</i>

630
00:46:02,840 --> 00:46:04,040
Mothulas…

631
00:46:04,120 --> 00:46:06,000
Yiaza, take our child inside.

632
00:46:10,800 --> 00:46:13,560
Layee, be careful.

633
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:34,240
It’s okay, Naka.
Your father will be back soon.

634
00:46:41,280 --> 00:46:42,280
Stop it.

635
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:43,840
-Why don't you go inside?
-Let go!

636
00:46:43,920 --> 00:46:45,520
-I'll kill every last Sawin!
-No!

637
00:46:45,600 --> 00:46:47,080
You can't, Auntie. You can't go.

638
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:48,320
-Khengla, the knife.
-Let go!

639
00:46:48,400 --> 00:46:50,040
-Watch the knife.
-Let me go.

640
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:51,280
Put it down.

641
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:52,560
Now.

642
00:46:54,360 --> 00:46:56,560
-Go up, Auntie.
-Go!

643
00:46:56,640 --> 00:46:57,800
Go up first.

644
00:47:06,880 --> 00:47:07,760
Dad.

645
00:47:07,840 --> 00:47:08,920
It’s me.

646
00:47:10,440 --> 00:47:11,960
Have you heard any news?

647
00:47:12,720 --> 00:47:14,360
I’m not sure

648
00:47:14,440 --> 00:47:17,560
who attacked us either. Just be prepared.

649
00:47:17,640 --> 00:47:20,120
We might have to move at any moment.

650
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:21,480
Yes.

651
00:47:28,960 --> 00:47:30,640
It’s okay, Naka.

652
00:47:32,400 --> 00:47:35,560
Stay with Mommy. You’ll be safe.

653
00:47:47,720 --> 00:47:50,200
<i>If they're able to capture our village,</i>

654
00:47:50,960 --> 00:47:53,920
<i>smuggling narcotics into Thailand</i>

655
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:57,240
<i>through the Naka Mountain Range</i>
<i>will become easy.</i>

656
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:03,200
Those Mothula bastards.

657
00:48:09,120 --> 00:48:11,400
<i>Throughout three days of battle,</i>

658
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,800
<i>thousands of villagers prepared</i>
<i>to evacuate at any moment.</i>

659
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:17,520
<i>While the men went out to fight,</i>

660
00:48:18,120 --> 00:48:20,840
<i>the women picked up weapons</i>
<i>to defend themselves.</i>

661
00:48:36,080 --> 00:48:39,800
Kase female warriors,
we must be ready to fight.

662
00:48:40,400 --> 00:48:42,680
While our male warriors
go out to drive off the enemy,

663
00:48:42,760 --> 00:48:46,080
we all need to
be ready to protect our home.

664
00:48:46,160 --> 00:48:48,400
Don't allow them to set foot in here.

665
00:48:48,480 --> 00:48:50,960
We will gladly die for our Kase.

666
00:48:51,480 --> 00:48:52,360
For Kase!

667
00:48:52,440 --> 00:48:53,720
For Kase!

668
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:55,240
For Kase!

669
00:48:55,320 --> 00:48:56,760
For Kase!

670
00:49:06,760 --> 00:49:09,760
<i>For three days and three nights,</i>
<i>we knew no peace.</i>

671
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:14,960
<i>But the terrible storm finally blew over</i>

672
00:49:15,040 --> 00:49:19,360
<i>when Colonel Layee</i>
<i>led our Kase warriors back.</i>

673
00:49:47,800 --> 00:49:48,920
I’m back, Yiaza.

674
00:50:00,560 --> 00:50:03,040
Naka. Daddy's home, Son.

675
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,800
I’m so foolish.

676
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:07,160
While everyone was
going through a life-or-death situation,

677
00:51:08,760 --> 00:51:11,080
I was here worrying
about my personal feelings.

678
00:51:15,520 --> 00:51:17,200
You don’t need to be sorry, Mintada.

679
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:21,640
I understand what it feels like

680
00:51:22,160 --> 00:51:23,360
when you love someone.

681
00:51:25,280 --> 00:51:28,880
You sound like an old man,
talking as if you've seen it all.

682
00:51:28,960 --> 00:51:31,200
I’ve been through it before, man.

683
00:51:31,960 --> 00:51:33,960
But you and I are different.

684
00:51:34,040 --> 00:51:36,360
Falling for a Kase girl is still possible.

685
00:51:37,200 --> 00:51:38,840
But falling for a Thai girl?

686
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:42,160
Two suns rising at once is more likely.

687
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:36,760
It's the exact same old story.

688
00:52:36,840 --> 00:52:37,760
No, it isn't.

689
00:52:39,200 --> 00:52:40,560
Haven't you ever heard?

690
00:52:40,640 --> 00:52:43,640
Before we ask for something,
we have to be the ones to give first.

691
00:52:48,280 --> 00:52:51,240
The people living out here are so remote

692
00:52:51,760 --> 00:52:53,560
they don't feel connected to us at all.

693
00:52:54,480 --> 00:52:57,120
So we have to make them feel

694
00:52:57,640 --> 00:52:58,880
that we’re one family.

695
00:53:51,680 --> 00:53:54,280
Done. Please don’t forget
to take care of your health.

696
00:53:55,040 --> 00:53:57,040
-Thank you.
-You’re welcome.

697
00:54:09,200 --> 00:54:10,920
You didn’t tell me you were coming.

698
00:54:12,360 --> 00:54:14,040
If I told you, I wouldn’t get to see

699
00:54:14,120 --> 00:54:17,280
if someone was flirting
with the local girls.

700
00:54:17,880 --> 00:54:19,080
Not a chance.

701
00:54:20,040 --> 00:54:20,960
Why is that?

702
00:54:21,880 --> 00:54:25,560
Well, I don't have a heart.
I can't love anyone else

703
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:29,320
because I already gave my heart to you.

704
00:54:39,760 --> 00:54:41,160
Please come in.

705
00:54:43,240 --> 00:54:44,200
What's your name?

706
00:54:54,360 --> 00:54:56,520
Please proceed to the table inside.

707
00:55:10,280 --> 00:55:12,880
<i>-Na na na, Na na na</i>
-Clap along!

708
00:55:12,960 --> 00:55:15,280
<i>Na na na, Na na na</i>

709
00:55:15,360 --> 00:55:17,000
Feel free to dance.

710
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:20,880
<i>Waking up in the morning</i>

711
00:55:20,960 --> 00:55:24,760
<i>Rubbing my eyes, washing my face</i>
<i>And brushing my teeth</i>

712
00:55:25,360 --> 00:55:27,920
<i>Doing this and that</i>

713
00:55:28,520 --> 00:55:32,520
<i>Doing that and this</i>
<i>Until the sun is high and late</i>

714
00:55:33,120 --> 00:55:35,360
<i>The school isn't far away…</i>

715
00:55:35,440 --> 00:55:39,040
Are you confident
this will win their hearts, Captain?

716
00:55:39,120 --> 00:55:42,400
<i>Many teachers…</i>

717
00:55:42,480 --> 00:55:44,280
I wouldn't say I'm confident, Chief.

718
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:47,000
But once I saw the situation,
I couldn't do nothing.

719
00:55:47,080 --> 00:55:50,760
If I hadn't come to see it, I'd never
have known what the villagers are lacking.

720
00:55:50,840 --> 00:55:52,720
Strange it took you this long to see it.

721
00:55:53,320 --> 00:55:56,240
Even the King
traveled all the way out here.

722
00:55:56,320 --> 00:55:59,720
If it weren't for Him,
our lives might be even worse.

723
00:56:00,520 --> 00:56:01,560
I promise you

724
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:04,680
that I will continue His Majesty's work

725
00:56:05,200 --> 00:56:06,600
with my entire life.

726
00:56:09,560 --> 00:56:10,960
<i>Calling all forest lovers.</i>

727
00:56:11,040 --> 00:56:13,200
<i>School's out and off we go!</i>

728
00:56:15,160 --> 00:56:17,640
Here we go.

729
00:56:17,720 --> 00:56:20,680
Where are you, Yoon, Nee?

730
00:56:21,360 --> 00:56:22,640
What are you doing, Mintada?

731
00:56:24,720 --> 00:56:25,800
BEWARE OF WILD ELEPHANTS

732
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:33,160
Don’t come any closer.

733
00:56:34,240 --> 00:56:35,480
Don’t!

734
00:56:36,040 --> 00:56:37,280
<i>We’re soaking wet like this.</i>

735
00:56:37,880 --> 00:56:40,880
<i>You’re a nurse, so you of all people know.</i>
<i>Don’t be stubborn.</i>

736
00:57:19,400 --> 00:57:21,480
Subtitle translation by:
Onamon Chaipramote
